est column definitions from the remote source, ensuring that your virtual table reflects any changes to the column structure in the remote database.  See: Create Virtual Tables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-24\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: T2502b\n\n--- Record 1177 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling  SAP Build Code\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, you can now use the generative-AI tools included in SAP Build Code to generate SQL statements in the SQL console that use customer-defined data models.  See: Use a Custom Data Model for AI-Powered SQL Generation  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-24\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: T2502b\n\n--- Record 1178 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Google Cloud Region\nDescription: SAP Document AI is now available in the Google Cloud region in30 - India (Mumbai).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1179 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.28.2. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1180 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Calculation Views\nDescription: In the calculation view editor, you can now create derived variables that dynamically retrieve values from\",805\n787,\"--- Record 601 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configure Navigation Link on Steps\nDescription: You can now configure navigation link on steps to navigate to specific pages for additional details.See Configure Step Navigation Link.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 602 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space of SAP Business Application Studio, the database module generator now supports binding new database modules to SAP HANA Cloud multi-tenant HDI container services.   See Create a New Business Application Project. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 603 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space of SAP Business Application Studio, additional SQL Console settings are now available to customize command separation, date and decimal formats, NULL display, result formatting, fractional digits, and the result set limit.  See User Preferences for SAP HANA Native Application Development Tools. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 604 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space of SAP Business Application Studio, the database module generator now includes an Advanced Settings option to configure deployment parameters such as stop on error, warning handling, and tracing. The selected options are written to the module’s package.json, enabling easier control of deployment behavior.  See Create a New Business Application Project. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 605 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, the Dependency Viewer now allows you to perform the following new actions:    Expand or collapse all schemas in the dependency graph  Locate and focus on objects with the predictive search box    See View Database Objects with the Database Explorer. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 606 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, the Explain Plan option in the SQL Console now shows data from both EXPLAIN_PLAN_TABLE and EXPLAIN_CALL_PLANS, providing a more complete view for SELECT statements that internally call procedures or calculation views.  See Use the SQL Console for SAP HANA to Query the Database. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 607 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Build Code, you can now generate realistic sample data for